  message: "Re-checked 2026-09-03 on dev 7cf2cf411a, after WI-vutav's receiver hop and\nWI-suhug's writer classifier landed, because rule 1 says the fix may already\nexist. It does not. Fixture `c := exec.Command(name, args...); c.Start();\nc.StdoutPipe()` still emits `go:external:0-0:Start:unresolved` and\n`go:external:0-0:StdoutPipe:unresolved`: the receiver hop STAMPS\nio_target_kind on the edge, it does not fill the module slot, so there is\nstill no effect-call row to anchor an ordering test on. Remedy (3) stays\nblocked on exactly what the 09-02 entry said. Nothing else on this item moved."  # 734e
- op: discuss  # 22cf
  at: '2026-09-03T19:01:18Z'  # 22cf
  by: agent  # 22cf
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 22cf
  clock: 5  # 22cf
  nonce: 22cf  # 22cf
  message: "CORRECTION TO THE 09-02 ENTRY, and the dependency it withheld. That entry said\nremedy (3) waits on \"resolving a receiver's type from its local binding\" and\nthat I had not established WHICH item owns the general form, so no isbefore\nedge was recorded. The owner had been on the tracker since 08-29: WI-lalot, a\nlibrary-signature catalogue (producing function -> returned type), filed from\nWI-doluf's cross-language check with its shape already ruled (separate from\nio_primitives; consumed by the existing var_types / return-type registry path).\nRule 1 -- check the tracker before building or deferring -- was not followed.\n\nWHY WI-lalot AND NOT \"RECEIVER TYPING\" IN GENERAL. WI-doluf (done, PR #635)\nalready carries an INFERRED type into the module slot for go, end to end: an\nin-repo factory returning net.Conn classifies net.Conn.Read. What it disclosed\nas out of reach is the LIBRARY case -- the registry is built from analysed\ndeclarations, so a receiver bound to a stdlib call has nothing to register.\nThat is exactly this item's blocker. Re-measured 2026-09-03 on dev 68db7bd6e5,\none fixture:\n\n    ln, _ := net.Listen(...)  ; ln.Accept()     -> go:external:0-0:Accept\n    conn, _ := ln.Accept()    ; conn.Read(buf)   -> go:external:0-0:Read\n    c := exec.Command(\"x\")    ; c.Start()        -> go:external:0-0:Start\n                              ; c.StdoutPipe()   -> go:external:0-0:StdoutPipe\n\nThe missing input is DATA (exec.Command -> *os/exec.Cmd is one row of\nWI-lalot), not another inference mechanism. WI-papar (rust, the `?` / chained\ncarry) is the same INV-linub class but a different shape and a different\nlanguage; it is not on this item's path.\n\nSEQUENCE, recorded as an isbefore edge from WI-lalot to this item: a go-first\nslice of WI-lalot (os/exec, net, bufio, net/http producers), then the\neffect-call ordering test under the two standing constraints (Finding A:\nkey on the GROUP marker; Finding B: exempt or record call_lines truncation).\nNothing else on this item moved."  # 22cf
- op: discuss  # c318
  at: '2026-09-04T13:29:01Z'  # c318
  by: agent  # c318
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c318
  clock: 6  # c318
  nonce: c318  # c318
  message: "THE BLOCKER THIS ITEM RECORDED IS REMOVED. Its 2026-09-03 entry reads:\n\n    Fixture `c := exec.Command(name, args...); c.Start(); c.StdoutPipe()` still emits\n    `go:external:0-0:Start:unresolved` and `go:external:0-0:StdoutPipe:unresolved`: the\n    receiver hop STAMPS io_target_kind on the edge, it does not fill the module slot, so\n    there is still no effect-call row to anchor an ordering test on. Remedy (3) stays\n    blocked on exactly what the 09-02 entry said.\n\nRe-run on that EXACT fixture after WI-lalot shipped:\n\n    go:os/exec:0-0:Start:unresolved\n    go:os/exec:0-0:StdoutPipe:unresolved\n\nBoth now carry a real module. WI-lalot supplied the missing fact (`exec.Command` returns\n`exec.Cmd`) AND the go lookup change without which the fact could not be consumed: go\nconsults its return-type registry for a BARE call and for a method on a TYPED variable,\nbut a package-qualified producer takes the selector branch, where `net` / `exec` is a\npackage rather than a variable, so `func_vars.get(...)` was empty and the registry was\nnever asked. The catalogue merge alone was inert.\n\nWHAT THIS ITEM STILL OWES, UNCHANGED. Step 1 (the census) is done: 1 of 14 rows true\n(7.1%), and the loop defence REFUTED at 0 of 14. Step 2 -- can the walk distinguish \"sink\nprecedes source with no loop enclosing either\" from \"inside a loop\" -- is still open, and\nstep 3's remedy is verdict-NEUTRALITY (report the row, do not let it move a verdict from\ninconclusive to violated), not removal, because 7.1% is not ~0.\n\nA CAUTION FOR WHOEVER TAKES STEP 3, carried over from WI-lalot's own measurement: WI-lalot\nmoved 317 call sites off the `external` sentinel on caddy + gocryptfs with 0 regressions\nand moved io-boundaries by ZERO, because the io classifier was already matching those\nmethods by short name. So \"the module slot is now filled\" does NOT by itself imply a new\nfinding appears; whether the ordering test this item wants can actually anchor on these\nedges needs its own measurement rather than inference from the slot being populated."  # c318
